情境主义者是谁，或是什么？排斥与包容的创伤一直是一种壮观的干扰。只有多样性，去殖民化的蚂蚁，无策略的群体，昆虫般的高速公路穿透壮观时间的屏障。它们既无历史也无终结，既无记忆也无启示，既无意外也无计划，没有线条，没有点，没有无限循环。既无前瞻性计划也无自发燃烧，而是在视线之外、意识之外的精心设计。难以察觉的变异，在幕后等待，就在舞台边缘。

政客们称他们为革命者，将他们塑造成有脸有名的个体，把这些具有传染性的物质网络编码成可接受的人类形式。

但他们一直是战术机器，未来的原住民入侵过去，交换位置，互换代码，无休止地复制由无源无终的微观情境所设计。群体总是在脸上飞舞；屏幕背后是活动的蜂巢。

他们一直在创造情境，而非以学术或其他分离的方式被动地识别它们。一直如此。而你以为这已经结束了。以为这是一个遗产、继承的问题，与过去的其他东西一起被传承下来。以为我们今天聚集在这里是为了聆听遗嘱的宣读。

Is it who, or what, are the situationists? The trauma of exclusions and inclusions was always a spectacular distraction. Only multiplicities, decolonized ants, swarms without strategies, insectoid freeways burrowed through the screens of spectacular time. They have neither history nor its end, neither memory nor apocalypse, neither accidents nor plans, no lines, no points, no infinite loops. No forward plans and no spontaneous combustion, but careful engineerings, out of sight, out of mind. Imperceptible mutations, waiting in the  wings, just off stage. 

The politicians called them revolutionaries, made them persons,with faces and names, coded these meshes of contagious matters into acceptable human forms.

But they were always tactical machines, natives of the future hacking into the past, trading places, swapping codes, endless replications of micro-situations engineered without sources or ends. Flocks are always flying in the  faces; hives of activity behind the screens. 

They have been making situations, as opposed to passively recogniz­ing them in academic or other separate terms. All this time. And you thought it was done. That this was a    matter of leg  acy, inheritance, something passed down  with  the rest of the past. That we were gathered here today to hear the reading of the will.

